  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final v28 text keeps 5% in S2 only as a review-and-remediation trigger with no sales stop, and S5's 8-per-100k threshold triggers assessment and notice but never a mandatory recall, so the two flagship-driven weaknesses (Hearth 10 and Ember 8) are both neutralised. Customers receive per-model numeric failure rates and sample sizes, but these are not published to the general public. S3 and S4 use 36-month new-unit deadlines and a 6-year retrofit window with an open 'where technically feasible' escape."
